    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "Stale Tip Relay (BIP 332) tracking issue",
    "body": "[BIP 332](https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0332.md) adds an optional `staletip` P2P message for announcing recent stale chain tips to peers that negotiated it via BIP 434.\n\nFull branch: https://github.com/pseudoramdom/bitcoin/tree/bip332-staletip-relay\nDiscussion: https://groups.google.com/g/bitcoindev/c/AwOPNxF15mU\n\n## Plan\n\n### Implementation\n\n- [ ] **PR 1 - Local tracking and RPC** https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36919\n  - Validation notification, report cached stale tips in RPC.\n  - No P2P change\n- [ ] **PR 2 - Headers-mode relay** https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36920\n  - `staletip` message, BIP 434 negotiation.\n  - Relays headers only, enough to observe stale rates.\n- [ ] **PR 3 - Stale-branch blocks**\n  - Serve available blocks on tracked stale branches\n  - `-staletips=blocks` additionally downloads them, as best-effort requests.\n- [ ] Fuzz tests\n- [ ] Release note and `doc/bips.md` entry\n- [ ] Update the reference implementation link in the BIP\n\n### Live tests\n  - [x] Regtest simulation - https://github.com/pseudoramdom/staletip-lab\n  - [ ] Mainnet\n  - [x] Signet\n      - Demo - https://staletip-signet.pseudoramdom.com\n  - [x] Testnet5 - https://github.com/pseudoramdom/bitcoin/tree/bip332-staletip-relay-testnet5\n     - Demo - https://staletip-testnet5.pseudoramdom.com\n\n## Open questions\n- [ ] Does relaying stale block data affect mining incentives? See the [mailing list discussion](https://groups.google.com/g/bitcoindev/c/AwOPNxF15mU)\n\n---\nCollaborators - @ajtowns @w0xlt ",
