      "updated_at": "2026-11-17T20:46:29Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "@ajtowns pointed out that the signet variant rule in BIP 332, and in the current implementation, isn’t enough.\n\nOn signet, BIP 332 treats two blocks as variants when they have the same previous block and header merkle root. The BIP 325 signature doesn’t cover the signet solution, though. So anyone holding one signed block can change the solution and re-grind PoW, which gives them unlimited valid variants. Those can push real stale tips out of the tracker. This only affects signet.\n\nThe fix is to compare the BIP 325 signet merkle root instead of the header merkle root. A follow-up PR will update the BIP and the implementation.\n\nWIP: https://github.com/pseudoramdom/bitcoin/tree/bip332-signet-state",
